-- title:
--   Kaimanovich–Vershik, Derriennic (as Erschler–Zheng apply it, p. 10) — the entropy criterion: the Poisson boundary is trivial iff h_μ = 0
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be a countable group and $\mu$ a probability on $\Gamma$ (`IsProbability`) of finite entropy (`HasFiniteEntropy`). Then the Poisson boundary of $(\Gamma, \mu)$ is trivial, `¬ HasNontrivialPoissonBoundary μ` (every bounded $\mu$-harmonic function $f : \Gamma \to \mathbb R$ is constant on the submonoid generated by the support of $\mu$), if and only if the asymptotic entropy $\mathbf h_\mu = \lim_n H(\mu^{(n)})/n$ (`asymptoticEntropy μ`) is $0$.
--
--   Erschler and Zheng, p. 10: “The entropy criterion of Kaimanovich-Vershik [36] and Derriennic [23], states that for $\mu$ of finite entropy, all bounded $\mu$-harmonic functions are constant if and only if the Avez asymptotic entropy $\mathbf h_\mu = 0$.”
--
--   The condition “all bounded $\mu$-harmonic functions are constant” is read as triviality of the Poisson boundary, the form in which p. 11 applies the criterion (“By the entropy criterion, non-triviality of Poisson boundary of $(G, \mu)$ is equivalent to $\mathbf h > 0$.”), with triviality as defined in the bundle note.
-- source:
--   Kaimanovich, V. A. and Vershik, A. M., Random walks on discrete groups: boundary and entropy, Ann. Probab. 11 (1983) 457–490, https://doi.org/10.1214/aop/1176993497, p. 10, the entropy criterion, and Derriennic, Y., Quelques applications du théorème ergodique sous-additif, Astérisque 74 (1980) 183–201 (no DOI), as applied in Erschler, A. and Zheng, T., Growth of periodic Grigorchuk groups, Invent. Math. 219 (2020) 1069–1155, https://doi.org/10.1007/s00222-019-00922-0 (arXiv:1802.09077v2, whose page numbers are used), p. 10

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ErschlerZheng_Walks
open ErschlerZheng

namespace KaimanovichVershik

theorem not_hasNontrivialPoissonBoundary_iff_asymptoticEntropy_eq_zero {Γ : Type*} [Group Γ]
    [Countable Γ] (μ : Γ → ℝ) (hμ : IsProbability μ) (hH : HasFiniteEntropy μ) :
    ¬ HasNontrivialPoissonBoundary μ ↔ asymptoticEntropy μ = 0 := by
  sorry

end KaimanovichVershik
